senses.gloss:
(I)--a Vasu worshipped for tejas;
1: भा. II. 3. 3; XI. २६. 3.
wife उषा who bore three sons, व्युष्ठ, रोचिष and आतप;
2: Ib. VI. 6. ११ and १६.
fought with महिष in the देवासुर war.
3: Ib. VIII. १०. ३२.

(II)--a son of विश्रवस् and कैकशी, and a friend of राम. On the advice of राम, performed funeral rites to his kith and kin, according to established conventions. Was made king of लन्का by राम. Held the चामर when Bharata carried पादुका of राम;
1: भा. IV. 1. ३७; IX. १०. १६, २९ and ४३.
knew the yoga power of Hari and attained salvation by सत्सन्ग; of superior bhakti;
2: Ib. II. 7. ४५; XI. १२. 5; Br. III. ३४. ३९.
a brother of रावण;
3: Ib. III. 8. ४७.
was present at राम's अभिषेक।
4: Vi. IV. 4. ९९.

--in honour of विष्णु; in the months of कार्तिक, Caitra, वैशाख, मार्गशीर्ष, फाल्गुण and आषा- ढ; gift of a gold fish recommended; the end of the year must close with लवन पर्वत दान; the ten अवतार्स् of Hari with दत्तात्रेय and व्यास to be worshipped;
1: M. ९९. 1-२१.
was observed by the courtesan अनन्गवती who became the queen of God of Love;
2: Ib. १००. १८-32.
doing it on the banks of the Ganges gives one निर्वाण।
3: Ib. १००. ३३.
